<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30525" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nausĕo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. n.
		nausea, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to be sea-sick</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 1,
				93</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si sine vomitu nauseavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 1,
					3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to be
			squeamish</i> or <i>qualmish, to vomit</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quidlibet, modo ne nauseet, faciat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 34, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ructantem et nauseantem Antonium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 12, 25, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 433</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To belch forth</i>, i. e. <i>give vent
				to, utter</i> nonsense: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ista effutientem nauseare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 30, 84</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To cause disgust</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc illis dictum est, qui stultitiā
					nauseant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4, 7, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
